  "notes": [
    "Generation provenance: claude-opus-5-5[1m] at reasoning effort high.",
    "Checks: tools/tpt source-library validate (valid, bindings=4082); proper-chronology record --check and annotations --check (current, orientation-v2); scripts/_proper_study.py check --phase research (exit 0); the research seal command computes (exit 0). make check-sources fails only at check-publication-inventories (claude-publications-v1.toml stale for the leaf and owner files changed here) and the source-family-migration check reports its pinned canonical_catalog_snapshot stale (new library records); both need tools/tpt source-inventory refresh / source-family-migration refresh, which rewrite shared inventories and were not run. check-source-containment and check-commentator-inventories pass.",
    "Outside research/: proper-components.toml now declares chronology_presentation = \"orientation-v2\" (one value and one comment word). tools/tpt proper-chronology refuses --presentation orientation-v2 while the manifest declares v1, so the packet's generation step required it; author-study needs v2 anyway. No element key changed: `acclamation` kept per context.md.",
    "Week XXIX owner additions 2-4 corrected to the registered page images (including the III.xvi quotation: the first record's 'ea' is not on the page). instance/manifest.md, propers/verified.md, review-dependencies.toml updated; context.md not edited by this stage.",
    "New fact for authors: Wilson p. 229 apparatus records the Vatican MS reading maiestatem tuam at III.ix, so the study's 'recurs, again word for word' holds only for Wilson's text; and the study's statement that Schuster and Fromage were read only in a text layer is now false (scope.md section 11).",
    "Feltoe's complete Verona scan (19,868,448 bytes) is registered as a tracked payload under the library's retain-locally default (precedent: the 28.6 MB tracked Wilson 1915 scan); the other new payloads are page excerpts (about 4.9 MB together). Wilson's parent PDF is remote because its first page is Google's digitisation notice; Lewis and Short (Harper issue, LoC copy) remote for 380 MB; an OUP 1984 impression read first was not registered (all rights reserved).",
    "Direct USCCB requests (GIRM, readings page) met the 15,748-byte challenge page; it was not circumvented. One early probe of GIRM ch. VII returned HTTP 200 (58,214 bytes) but was not saved and is not relied on.",
    "Independence: the GPT leaf for this identity, its PDFs/web edition and its review directory were not opened, and no search printed a line from them; only provider-neutral src/sources records were used."
  ],
